  All too often, a recurring scenario develops where there is not enough time in the day or enough physicians to manage the work load of an elective practice and cover the hospital.   The hospital needs the trauma and/or comprehensive stroke center covered but the surgeons are either busy in clinic or in an elective case; unavailable when needed.  The hospital tries to recruit to fill the gap but there just isn’t enough elective work to keep everyone happy.  Or worse yet, the hospital tries to employ their own physicians only to find out that they can’t find enough to cover and the private physicians feel threatened and take their cases elsewhere.

